# Database / Prisma rules

- Inspect the existing Prisma schema first (`backend/prisma/schema.prisma`).
- Reuse existing models and relations when appropriate.
- Avoid unnecessary schema changes.
- Schema changes must be justified by **approved** functionality.
- Create migrations only when genuinely required.
- Never modify or destroy existing data unnecessarily.
- Do not make database changes merely for convenience.
- When schema work is approved and applied, verify migrations and Prisma client generation as applicable.

Prefer additive models/fields over rewriting existing tables or enums unless explicitly approved.
